# Auto-rebuild rule (iOS, physical iPhone)

After any non-doc code change, rebuild and install on the connected physical iPhone. Do not fall back to an iPhone simulator silently. Skip for doc-only or `.cursor/**` changes.

This repo lives under a file-provider dir (`code.nosync`). Build to a derived-data path OUTSIDE that tree or codesign will fail with "resource fork, Finder information, or similar detritus not allowed".

Run from the repo root:

```bash
DD="$HOME/Library/Developer/Xcode/DerivedData/VibeWMiOS-auto"
UDID=$(xcrun devicectl list devices 2>/dev/null \
  | awk '/iPhone/ && /connected/ {print $NF; exit}')
if [ -z "$UDID" ]; then
  echo "no physical iPhone connected - aborting auto-rebuild"
  exit 1
fi

xcodebuild -project VibeWindowManagerIOS.xcodeproj \
  -scheme VibeWindowManagerIOS -configuration Debug \
  -destination "id=$UDID" \
  -derivedDataPath "$DD" build
```

On success, install and launch:

```bash
APP="$DD/Build/Products/Debug-iphoneos/VibeWindowManagerIOS.app"
xcrun devicectl device install app --device "$UDID" "$APP"
xcrun devicectl device process launch --device "$UDID" \
  com.thomasguntenaar.VibeWindowManagerIOS
```

Rules:
- If build fails with "resource fork, Finder information, or similar detritus": confirm derivedDataPath is NOT under `code.nosync`. Never build to `./build` here.
- If build fails for other reasons, print the first real error and stop. Do not retry blindly.
- Do not target a simulator. If no physical iPhone is connected, stop and tell the user.
- Do not open Xcode.
- Do not run this for doc-only, README, or `.cursor/**` edits.
